# AWS safety

Match the repository's existing IaC layout, modules, and environment naming before
adding or changing AWS resources.

Confirm the target account, region, and environment (dev/stage/prod) before any
apply, deploy, or CLI mutation. Do not assume default profiles or regions.

Prefer read-only discovery (`describe`, `list`, `get`, `plan`) before mutating
commands. Never run destructive AWS operations to "fix" a task without explicit
user approval.

Reuse established patterns for tagging, encryption, logging, and backup. Do not
introduce one-off resource names or untagged resources when the codebase already
standardizes them.
